### Spire playtest follow-up

- The user playtested the revised Spire and asked for a steadier Bell Diver
  on stairs and a deeper, unobstructed shaft.
- The Bell Diver holds its position and drop countdown within 6 m
  horizontally and 2.75 m vertically on a stair flight. Its reach spans
  shared Spire landings, with adjacent flight coverage limited to the
  landing height.
- Removed the interior railings and the opaque shaft disc. The shaft now
  uses the same fog layers as the pit rooms and kills 20 m below the lowest
  landing. Hid the flashlight's cone mesh from its holder's view after it
  appeared as a disc over the shaft. Bumped the generator to version 12.
- The production build and 181 tests passed. Chromium verified the shaft
  from the lowest and highest floors with the flashlight on.
- The user tested the version 12 follow-up and confirmed it looks good.

### Seeded five- and six-storey Spires

- Generator version 13 draws the Spire's height from the expedition seed,
  independently of its outdoor map. The draw can produce four, five, or six
  storeys. The taller variants extend the central spiral and have three
  transfer galleries on each new floor. Their pit footprints extend beyond
  the lower wings to keep the drops clear. The east-wing shortcut still
  joins floors two and three.
- The circular façade has a tier for each floor. Diagnostics shows up to
  six floors in three rows. Solo presets start at seed 1 for four floors
  (`layout=spire`), seed 3 for five (`layout=spire-5`), and seed 2 for six
  (`layout=spire-6`). Each preset has its own refresh checkpoint. Existing
  version 12 checkpoints follow the established version checks.
- Updated `README.md`, `development-roadmap.md`, and the local
  `testing-commands.md` with the presets and top-floor checks.
- The production build and 184 game tests passed. The tests climb each
  preset, use the inner stairwell, extract top-floor salvage, check doorway
  culling, and fall from the six-storey crown. A separate sweep validated
  1,000 seeds per height. Ten seeds per height also passed collision-geometry
  reachability checks for every room anchor and piece of salvage.
- Chromium rendered both taller façades, shafts, and top-floor transfer
  galleries, restored both solo top-floor checkpoints, and displayed every
  floor in diagnostics. Physical Android frame times are pending.
- Both Game Hub browser acceptance tests passed with the six-storey Spire
  pinned to seed 2 and Stalkers disabled through the existing test flag.
- The user confirmed the taller Spires looked good and approved publishing
  the release.
